      "project_health": "Green 7/13/26: The project continues to move in the right direction. IC continues to meet with Cutler Bay on a regular cadence, and the client remains engaged in project activities. The implementation is a relatively straightforward setup, with the primary focus areas currently are eReviews, Bluebeam integration, and GIS. The client continues to test as configurations are completed, and the project is transitioning toward more formal testing activities. A PO has been issued for Bluebeam licenses, and the client is following up internally to confirm purchase completion. Payment setup is underway. Conversion remains an area requiring additional attention. Cutler Bay submitted their mapping document on June 12, and Conversion continues to work through outstanding items and updates needed within the mapping document. As of July 2, there were still several items requiring correction. Karen, IC, and myself met to review the outstanding items, and IC provided additional feedback to Conversion. At this time, we do not yet have a confirmed timeline for completion of the mapping document or when the first conversion pass can be returned. Daily follow-ups with conversion 6/9/26: The client is currently working on completing the 1st conversion mapping document. | Karen Churchill is the assigned engineer | The mapping document is due to be uploaded to Kiteworks by June 12, and the client has indicated they do not foresee any issues meeting that deadline. | The client is currently working through charge codes and is seeking clarification from IC regarding the required completion date. This will be discussed during sessions the week of 6/9/26 | Payments activities are in progress. A meeting was held with the client team and Laurie on May 29th. Laurie provided the information and requirements needed from the client to move forward with the Chase setup process. | At this time, the client has not yet returned the requested information to Laurie. | GIS integration is working, but the client needs to update setup a new map server. | The team (myself and IC included) is seeking clarification regarding ReadyForms, as it is included in the client\u2019s contract. | The client anticipates needing 1-2 custom reports for EPL, and plans to discuss reporting requirements during a July meeting they are having to include all the custom report they have identified for all their modules. | Bluebeam implementation activities are underway. | TCM conversion; this was not included in the original contract scope.Chris DeRoche is preparing a quote for the requested TCM conversion work. Current discussions indicate the TCM conversion would likely be completed as a post-go-live effort. | The project remains on track for the onsite October 20th go-live date. | Tyler PM is working with Nick and Greg to draft a formal conversion acknowledgment document for the client. Nick has already provided initial feedback on the acknowledgment document, we just need to review before sending to the client. | The implementation plan includes 5 conversion passes. | The client has stated that the October 20th go-live date is firm and will proceed regardless of conversion outcomes. | The client would like to pursue conversion efforts but has indicated that if they are not satisfied with the results by the 5th conversion pass, they will proceed with go-live without conversion data. 3/3/26: Cutler Bay would like to pursue a conversion with the expectation that they can abandon it if it isn\u2019t ready for their 10/19/26 go-live. They need to be live by Jan 1 (funding deadline).",
